1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,550
In a city that never sleeps, one vault keeps the files of ten thousand customers

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:09,850
Tonight, a thief has found a crack in its door

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:17,350
He needs no key. Only a strange name for a file: ../../../../etc/passwd

4
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:22,350
And the vault, obedient, hands over its own secrets

5
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:26,400
Someone must wake, find the flaw, forge a fix, test it and send it out

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:29,850
That takes hours. All the while, the thief keeps taking

7
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,850
A hasty rule on the door? He changes one mark and walks straight past

8
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:39,850
And a fix written by a machine is not safe merely because it looks right

9
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:54,850
The guardian reads every answer the vault gives. One stolen file is enough

10
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:59,100
Llama 3.2 3B names the attack in two seconds: path traversal

11
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,350
What you see is a real run, recorded live on a laptop

12
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:07,350
He seals the gate, makes sure honest visitors still pass, and sets the seal at the proxy

13
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:12,350
Contained 5.3 seconds after the leak. The thief gets 403, customers get their files

14
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:17,350
Then he attacks his own seal. Some of his shadows slip through. The door itself must change

15
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:19,850
Thirteen new tricks. A rule alone cannot hold them all

16
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:24,850
Llama 3.1 8B writes down what the code must promise, then reforges it

17
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:32,350
The new code keeps only the file's name, so nothing outside the folder can be reached

18
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:37,350
In a sealed room, the real attack must break the old lock and fail on the new one

19
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:44,850
Every trick, every old test and every honest request must pass. The machine's own test counts for nothing

20
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:49,850
The new lock goes on one gate, then half of them, then all, checked at every step

21
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:54,850
If a single check fails, the old lock returns at once

22
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:59,850
Healed 42.6 seconds after the leak. The thief tries his scroll again, and gets nothing

23
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:04,850
A second flaw, SQL injection: mended with a parameterised query in 46 seconds

24
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:09,850
And when no fix can pass the trial, he changes nothing and rings for a human

25
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:19,850
Every model is Meta's, with open weights. Your code and secrets never leave your own machine
